  "name": "21 HYDROXYLASE ANTIBODIES SERUM",
  "code": "1730",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The <strong data-start=\"68\" data-end=\"95\">21-hydroxylase antibody</strong> test is used to detect <strong data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"171\">autoantibodies against the enzyme 21-hydroxylase</strong>, primarily in the context of <strong data-start=\"201\" data-end=\"237\">autoimmune adrenal insufficiency</strong>, most notably <strong data-start=\"252\" data-end=\"284\">Autoimmune Addison's disease</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"292\" data-end=\"316\"><strong data-start=\"296\" data-end=\"316\">Clinical Purpose</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"317\" data-end=\"627\">\n<li data-start=\"317\" data-end=\"456\">\n<p data-start=\"319\" data-end=\"456\">To aid in the <strong data-start=\"333\" data-end=\"372\">diagnosis of autoimmune adrenalitis</strong>, the most common cause of <strong data-start=\"399\" data-end=\"432\">primary adrenal insufficiency</strong> in developed countries.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"457\" data-end=\"627\">\n<p data-start=\"459\" data-end=\"627\">To evaluate patients with <strong data-start=\"485\" data-end=\"522\">unexplained adrenal insufficiency</strong>, <strong data-start=\"524\" data-end=\"568\">polyglandular autoimmune syndromes (APS)</strong>, or a <strong data-start=\"575\" data-end=\"593\">family history</strong> of autoimmune endocrine diseases.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
